These fall into the fairly expected realm of motion graphics — there are a lot of traditional “design” elements; there isn’t really a narrative. Formalisms are more likely to be from a design classroom that from any history of the screen. This is familiar to a designer — while the animating might be foreign, it’s not hard to think about how you might compose still bits of designs like this. These are all probably designed with after effects; shape layers, maybe a few type layers …

