This seems like a good example where the motion helps show the difference that they are trying to explain. And so that it is a motion graphic enhances the type specimen. Because you can see the transition from the beautiful version to the ugly version. So that seems like a really good reason to make something a motion graphic, to me. It's the same reason that we're using graphic design to better communicate something, it even is better communicating it than the print graphic version is, perhaps.

